  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Rebuild: Support for the MILF Amnesty Process</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project aims to contribute to addressing the root causes of conflict and violence in the Bangsamoro region by providing a pathway for individuals who have been involved in armed struggle to transition and transform into peaceful and productive members of the community. The proposed Project will seek to deliver the following outputs: (1) Provision of technical and operational support for the National Amnesty Commission and Local Amnesty Boards; and, (2) Provision of needs-based support for amnesty applicants and their families in completing the processes and requirements needed for amnesty applications, including legal and documentation missions for MILF amnesty applicants.The above initiatives are expected to contribute to the broader goal of achieving lasting stability and development in the BARMM and in the Philippines.</narrative>
  </description>
